-- title:
--   Frobenius re-basing of rigidifications acts by a central scalar
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are distinct primes, $N$ is a non-zero natural number with $r \nmid N$ (hypotheses `hrr`, `hrN`).
--
--   Coefficient rings. $\mathcal{O}$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is the fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$. Next, `Onr` is a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, and the group of hypotheses on it requires: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), maximality of that ideal (`hOnr_max`), that every element of `Onr` satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), that every monic polynomial over `Onr` of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and that $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   Quaternionic data. For rationals $a, b$, the hypothesis `hB` asserts that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and that, for each finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, the completion at $v$ is a division algebra precisely when $v$ divides $r$ or $\bar r$. $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ (`hΛ`: an order maximal among orders), all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` $: \Lambda \to \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \times \mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$ (Witt vectors over $\mathbb{F}_{r^2}$) satisfies `IsOrderCoord`: it is additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, is multiplicative for the twisted rule $(x_1,x_2)(y_1,y_2) = (x_1y_1 + r\,x_2\,\varphi(y_2),\; x_1y_2 + x_2\,\varphi(y_1))$ with $\varphi$ the Witt-vector Frobenius, is injective, has dense image in each $r$-adic truncation, and matches reduced traces with $x_1 + \varphi(x_1)$.
--
--   The base objects over the residue ring. $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$, $X_0$ is a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module (a two-dimensional commutative formal group with $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$-action and an element $\varpi$ with $\varpi \circ \varpi = [r]$) over that ring, of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ are two-variable formal coordinates along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀` asserts that $\theta_0$ are formal coordinates for the group law of $A_0$ identifying the formal completion with $X_0$ so that the action of $m \in \Lambda$ corresponds to $\mathrm{act}(\mathrm{coord}(m)_1) + \mathrm{act}(\mathrm{coord}(m)_2)\circ\varpi$.
--
--   The formal moduli side. $\iota : \mathbb{Z}_{r^2} \to \mathrm{Onr}$ is a ring homomorphism; $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`: its zero and one Lie pieces are complementary and invertible) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`). $M$ is a moduli package over $\mathrm{Onr}$ in the sense of the structure `ModuliPackage` (a functor on pairs consisting of a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent and a homomorphism $\mathrm{Onr} \to B$), and `hM` states that $M$ is a Zariski sheaf. The family $\eta$ assigns to each rigidified formal module $t$ over such a $B$ a point of $M$, and `hη` consists of three clauses: for Noetherian $B$, two admissible rigidified objects have the same image under $\eta$ if and only if they are isomorphic; $\eta$ commutes with base change along ring homomorphisms compatible with the legs, applied to admissible objects; and every point of $M$ over a Noetherian $B$ becomes, after passing to the members of a finite family of localisations covering $\mathrm{Spec}\,B$, the image under $\eta$ of an admissible rigidified object.
--
--   The matrix realisation. $E_0$ is a ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the set of $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$-action endomorphisms of $\Phi$ together with $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$, and `hE₀` states that $E_0$ is injective and that for some $m \in \mathbb{N}$ every matrix over $\mathcal{O}$ becomes, after multiplication by $r^{m}$, a value of $E_0$, while $r^{m}E_0(e)$ always comes from a matrix over $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   Comparison data. $\kappa : \mathrm{Onr}/(\pi) \to \mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ is a ring homomorphism compatible with the two quotient maps (`hκ`), $n_0 \in \mathbb{N}$, and $\beta_0$ is a pair of power series which is an isogeny $\Phi \to X_0 \otimes_\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   The dictionary. $\Xi$ assigns, to every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra leg $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$ in which $\pi$ acts nilpotently, and to every rigidified curve over $(B,\psi)$ — that is, a pair consisting of a fake elliptic curve $E/B$ of level $N$ with $\Lambda$-action and a rigidification $\rho$: a reduction $\rho.\mathrm{Eb}$ of $E$ modulo $\pi$, a pullback $\rho.\mathrm{Ab}$ of $A_0$ along the reduction of $\psi$, and an isogeny pair $\rho.\varphi, \rho.\varphi'$ of degree $r^{\rho.d}$ between them preserving the level structures — a $G$-point of $M$ over $B$, i.e. a leg $\mathrm{Onr} \to B$, a witness that $r$ is nilpotent, and a point of $M$ for that leg. Four hypotheses constrain $\Xi$: `hΞleg`, that over a $B$ whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$ the leg of $\Xi(x)$ is $\mathrm{Fr}^{k}$-twisted, $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$, for some $k \in \mathbb{Z}$; `hΞnat`, that $\Xi$ is compatible with base change along $\varphi : B \to B'$ whenever the curves and rigidifications are related by a pullback square (`FakeEllipticCurve.IsPullbackVia` and `Rigidification.IsPullbackVia`); `hΞiso`, that $\Xi$ takes equal values on two rigidified curves over the same $(B,\psi)$ whose underlying curves are isomorphic compatibly with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level (`IsoVia`), provided the rigidifications are comparable in the sense that there are maps $ib$ of the reductions and $uA$ of the $A_0$-pullbacks, commuting with the structure maps, and exponents $i_1, j_1$ with $ib$ followed by $\varphi'$, $uA$ and $[r^{i_1}]$ equal to $\varphi$ followed by $[r^{j_1}]$; and `hΞdef`, the defining recipe: over a $B$ with only trivial idempotents and $r$ nilpotent, for a rigidified curve $x$ carrying a formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ via `coord`, there are $j \le 1$ and a rigidified formal module $t$ over $B$ with $t.X = X$, which is the rigidification transport of $(\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0)$ along $\rho$ at level $j$, admissible for the twisted leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, and such that $\Xi(x)$ is the $G$-point with leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and underlying point $\eta(t)$.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses, for every Noetherian $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with leg $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$ such that the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and the only idempotents of $B$ are $0$ and $1$, for every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ of level $N$ with $\Lambda$-action and every rigidification $\rho$ of $E$ relative to $\psi$, both of the following hold.
--
--   First, there exist a rigidification $\rho_{+}$ of the same curve $E$ relative to the twisted leg $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and an integer $c$ such that three conditions hold. (i) The relation `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` holds for the central element $z^{c}$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, where $z$ is the image of the unit $r$ of $K_0$ under the scalar embedding into $M_2(K_0)$, and the two $G$-points $\Xi_{(B,\psi)}(E,\rho)$ and $\Xi_{(B,\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr})}(E,\rho_{+})$; unfolding, there are an element $e$ of the centraliser of the $\mathbb{Z}_{r^2}$-action and $\varpi$ on $\Phi$ and natural numbers $k, m'$ with $E_0(e) = r^{k}\,z^{-c}$, with $e$ having kernel of degree $r^{2m'}$, and with the predicate `IsTranslate` for $\iota, \Phi, \eta, \mathrm{Fr}$, the power series of $e$, $k$, $m'$ holding between those two $G$-points. (ii) For every prime $\ell \neq r$ whose image in $B$ is a unit, every extra level structure at $\ell$ on $A_0$ (the Lean binder here is again named `K₀`, shadowing the fraction field) and every two extra level structures $C, C'$ at $\ell$ on $E$: if $C$ is carried into the level of $A_0$ along $\rho$ — meaning that for every scheme $T$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(B/\pi B)$ and every point $R$ of $\rho.\mathrm{Eb}$ over it, factorisation of $R$ followed by $\rho.\mathrm{gb}$ through $C$ implies that $R$ followed by $\rho.\varphi$ and $\rho.\mathrm{gA}$ factors through the level of $A_0$ — and if $C'$ is carried into it in the same sense along $\rho_{+}$, then for every scheme $T$, every $t : T \to \mathrm{Spec}\,B$ and every point $R$ of $E$ over $t$, $R$ factors through $C$ if and only if it factors through $C'$. (iii) For every $n$ whose image in $B$ is a unit, every full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ and all full level-$n$ structures $P_n, P_n'$ on $E$ which are height-normalised transports of $P_0$ along $\rho$ and along $\rho_{+}$ respectively (`Rigidification.IsNormLevelTransport` for $\mathrm{Fr}, \theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \Phi, \iota, \mathrm{coord}$), one has the identity of sections $r^{c^{+}}\cdot P_n' = r^{(-c)^{+}}\cdot P_n$ in the group law of $E$ over the identity base, where $(\cdot)^{+}$ denotes the truncation `Int.toNat`; thus $r^{c}P_n' = P_n$ when $c \ge 0$ and $P_n' = r^{-c}P_n$ when $c \le 0$.
--
--   Second, the mirror statement: there exist a rigidification $\rho_{-}$ of $E$ relative to $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-1}$ and an integer $c$ satisfying the same three conditions (i), (ii), (iii), read with $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-1}$ and $\rho_{-}$ in place of $\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and $\rho_{+}$.
--
--   This is the Frobenius re-basing step in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description of the supersingular locus: twisting the leg $\psi$ by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\pm 1}$ replaces a rigidification of a fake elliptic curve by another rigidification of the same curve, and moves its point under the dictionary $\Xi$ only by a central scalar $r^{c}$, the accompanying level structures (extra level at primes $\ell \neq r$, and height-normalised full level) being matched accordingly. It is the single-step input to the iterated version [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_rigidification_frobTwist_zpow_isActBy_scalar_extraLevel_normLevel_of_rigidifiedToG`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_rigidification_frobTwist_zpow_isActBy_scalar_extraLevel_normLevel_of_rigidifiedToG) and is used in the labelling bijection [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.omega_family_bijective_label_of_isAlgClosed_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.omega_family_bijective_label_of_isAlgClosed_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr).
